{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.C1NewtonRamification","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1NewtonRamification","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Degree.Lemmas"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.dilationLift_pow_two_mul_add_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.dilationLift_pow_two_mul_add_one","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1NewtonRamification.lean#L165-L170","doc":"**Odd powers do not**: `c^{2k+1} = c·q^k`.  With\n`dilationLift_pow_two_mul` this says the group generated by the lift is\n`q^ℤ ⊔ c·q^ℤ` — index 2 over `q^ℤ`, i.e. the weight lattice is `½ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.dilationLift_pow_two_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.dilationLift_pow_two_mul","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1NewtonRamification.lean#L160-L163","doc":"**Even powers of the lift descend to the base**: `c^{2k} = q^k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.dilationLift_unique_up_to_sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.dilationLift_unique_up_to_sign","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1NewtonRamification.lean#L147-L158","doc":"**The lift is unique up to the deck sign.**  Two lifts of the dilation to the\nramified cover differ by `±1`, so the deck group `ℤ/2` is exactly the\nambiguity in the weight — no more, no less. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.not_isSquare_dilationFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.not_isSquare_dilationFactor","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1NewtonRamification.lean#L129-L145","doc":"**`q` is not a square in `ℚ[q]`.**  Same degree parity as\n`not_isSquare_newtonEdgeConstant`: `f² = q` would force `2·natDegree f = 1`.\n\nConsequence: the dilation `x ↦ q·x` does **not** lift to the slope-2 ramified\ncover over the base field — the lift requires adjoining `√q`.  So C1's `∞`\nweight cannot be a power of `q` with integer exponent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.not_isSquare_X_sub_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.not_isSquare_X_sub_one","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1NewtonRamification.lean#L77-L80","doc":"Restated in Mathlib's `IsSquare` form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.not_isSquare_newtonEdgeConstant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.not_isSquare_newtonEdgeConstant","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1NewtonRamification.lean#L60-L75","doc":"**The ramification is not removable.** `q − 1` is not a square in `ℚ[q]`:\n`f² = q − 1` would force `2·natDegree f = 1`, impossible. Hence the Newton-edge\nequation `q²t² = q − 1` has no solution `t` in `ℚ(q)` (the `q²` is already a\nsquare, so a solution there would give one here), and the slope-½ edge genuinely\nrequires adjoining `√(q−1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.newtonEdgeConstant_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.newtonEdgeConstant_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1NewtonRamification.lean#L57-L58","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.newtonEdgeConstant_natDegree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.newtonEdgeConstant_natDegree","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1NewtonRamification.lean#L54-L55","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.newtonEdgeConstant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.newtonEdgeConstant","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1NewtonRamification.lean#L49-L52","doc":"The Newton-edge characteristic polynomial in the unknown `t`, with the `q`-side\nwritten additively: the edge equation is `q²t² = (q−1)`, so after clearing the\n(already square) `q²` the question is whether `X − 1` is a square. ","signatureChunk":0}]}